================================================================================

This file lists third-party software that the Partner Platform depends on,
bundles, or redistributes, together with the licences that govern each item.

Scope and method
----------------
Licence identifiers below were taken from package metadata (Python distribution
metadata and npm registry `license` fields) and from licence files committed to
this repository. Where a package publishes a dual or compound licence, the full
expression is reproduced rather than simplified.

The Partner Platform links to all of its dependencies as unmodified libraries
resolved at install time; it does not vendor their source. Full licence texts
ship inside each package's own distribution.

The Python closure is hash-locked: `backend/requirements.lock` pins 71
distributions by version and SHA-256 and is installed with `--require-hashes`,
so the inventory below is exact for that file rather than an approximation of a
resolve. The Node closure is pinned by `frontend/package-lock.json`
(160 packages, production and build tooling combined).

Note that `requirements.lock`, not `requirements.txt`, is what the image
installs, and the two have drifted. Where they disagree, this file follows the
lock, because the lock is what ships. The drift is itemised in
THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md and tracked in SECURITY.md.

